cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this research prototype, please cite the software."
title: "EmbodiedSkill-ROS: Contract-Driven Reliable Skill Execution for ROS2 Robots"
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: "Fu"
    given-names: "Zhengqing"
version: 0.3.1
date-released: 2026-08-09
license: Apache-2.0
abstract: >-
  A contract-driven execution layer with epistemic robot state, generic repair,
  structural replanning, outcome verification, adversarial evaluation, and
  process-separated ROS2 Humble runtime validation. Version 0.3.0 adds an explicit
  skill, state, capability, and ROS transport integration boundary for an existing
  JAKA/Kargo robot stack. Version 0.3.1 adds portable CI, static-analysis baselines,
  release and contract consistency checks, canonical evidence protection, and
  executor audit documentation. No ROS2/JAKA execution semantics change in 0.3.1;
  its ROS2/JAKA evidence remains inherited from 0.3.0. The integration is validated
  against the external generated ROS schemas in a separate-process stub;
  vendor-backed node execution and robot hardware remain unverified.
